  "remaining_limitations": [
    "This report validates resources, selection and transform matrices; it does not establish pixel-level parity in the modern rendered client.",
    "GUI-only legacy transform conversion is deliberate for hidden book display models; physical item hand transforms are a separate pipeline.",
    "Static Golem Builder world fallback omits the TESR lava surface and moving press animation. Original blueprint creates a fresh, unticked tile (press=0); GolemPress bookmark uses its explicit GUI display stack.",
    "Imported world stone models use the first original random texture-rotation variant.",
    "Vanilla cells use Minecraft 1.21.1 block/fluid models. Their assets and lighting can differ from Minecraft 1.12.2 and require visual comparison.",
    "The historical thaumcraft:leather model remains unresolved in the import index; BookAssets maps that ingredient to minecraft:leather.",
    "Stateful recipe icon rendering must retain actual item components for color and dynamic overrides; empty original jar models alone cannot represent filled jars.",
    "Unregistered non-full world blocks still use an air neighbor proxy. Their original geometry is rendered, but exact neighbor AO/occlusion of those shapes is not yet represented.",
    "Infusion Matrix world preview currently uses the original static inventory geometry. Original BlockInfusionMatrix is invisible and the blueprint invokes an idle TileInfusionMatrixRenderer (eight ModelCube parts at offsets +/-0.25 and scale 0.45, with per-part quarter-turns). Its world gaps, rune orientation and TESR lighting are not yet exact; the original GUI inventory model remains correct."
  ],
